-- ==========================================
-- SMART AUTO FISH (v7)
-- ------------------------------------------
-- Panel: the KILLSTAM hub's look. Tabs on the left (fishing / shops / other), a LIVE
-- list of what is on, notices that slide in at the top. RightShift or the floating
-- SMART FISH button hides and shows it, the x button hides it, and "stop script"
-- on the third tab stops the script (the game's own auto fishing is left as it is).
-- Written against the game's own client code (see Modules/AutoFishing_lua,
-- Modules/ThrowCinematic_lua, Modules/HookMeter_lua, Modules/FishTag_lua,
-- Modules/ThrowRod_lua, Modules/Settings_lua, Modules/Upgrades_lua, Modules/Rods_lua,
-- Modules/Baits_lua, Modules/ConsumeBait_lua, Modules/NPC_Sell_lua, Modules/Touch_UI_lua,
-- Modules/IdleRejoin_lua):
--   * Auto Fish     -> runs the game's built-in auto fishing loop (cast, aim, catch,
--                      reel), started with the same AutoFishing:Toggle() call as its
--                      own footer button.
--   * Perfect Cast  -> the built-in auto releases the cast at a random spot on the
--                      hook meter. This waits until the arrow is in the middle of the
--                      green zone (the spot the game itself draws as "Perfect") and
--                      releases there, every cast.
--   * Best Fish     -> aims at the most expensive fish instead of a random one, priced
--                      with the same GetSellValue call as the $ tags on the fish.
--   * Quick Reel    -> the game only reels in once the hook is full or nothing is left
--                      above it. This reels in as soon as the most expensive fish is on
--                      the hook, staying only for finds and for fish worth at least a
--                      quarter of it.
--   * Skip Cutscene -> sets the game's own Settings > "Rare Catch Cutscene" to None, so
--                      rare catches skip the showcase. It is a saved game setting: it
--                      stays after the panel is closed (this button or the game's
--                      Settings menu turns it back on).
--   * Auto Upgrade  -> in the rod / upgrade shop, with cash (never Robux): buys the
--                      luckiest rod you can afford that beats yours and equips it, and
--                      the upgrades (Capacity / Strength / Weight / Bounce), cheapest first.
--   * Auto Bait     -> keeps a bait active by using the best bait you own; in the bait
--                      shop it buys up to 20, each costing at most a fifth of what its 5
--                      casts usually catch, and on a Sell Trip at most a fifth of what
--                      the trip sold (the rest is saved up for rods and upgrades).
--   * Sell Trip     -> once 250 unlocked fish are in the bag (or it is full), walks to the
--                      sell NPC and uses its "Sell All Fish", walks through the shops that
--                      have something to buy, then back to the water and fishes on.
--                      It walks like you would (no teleporting); the game sells instant
--                      selling as its "Auto Sell" gamepass, which this does not copy.
--   * Overnight     -> after 15 minutes without input the game moves you to a server
--                      (IdleRejoin). Put this file in Volt's autoexec folder so it runs
--                      again there; it then walks back to the water and fishes on.
--   * Auto Fight    -> plays the "Click Fast" catch fight for rare fish, under the
--                      game's own CatchFight.MaxClickRate.
--   * Rod           -> puts your rod back in your hand while auto fishing is on.
-- The server times every throw itself (flight, dive, catch window, return) and only
-- pays for fish hooked during the catch window, so a cast cannot be skipped outright;
-- Quick Reel and Skip Cutscene cut the waiting inside it.
-- Needs: Level 5 (the game's rule) and standing at the water.
-- Nothing on screen? Look in the Volt console (not Roblox F9) for lines starting with [SmartAutoFish].
-- ==========================================

local function say(text)
    print("[SmartAutoFish] " .. text)
end

